	title = {Artificital Intelligence-Assisted Blockchain-Software Defined Cloud-Based Secure Data Exchange in Industrial IoT Frameworks},
	year = {2025},
	pages = {},
	doi = {10.1109/ICDSNS65743.2025.11168671},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-105019062456&doi=10.1109%2FICDSNS65743.2025.11168671&partnerID=40&md5=207744fee7d8da8dbc431994060e1ebb},
	affiliations = {Nitte Meenakshi Institute of Technology, Department of Artificial Intelligence and Data Science, Bengaluru, India; The Islamic University, Najaf, Department of Computers Techniques Engineering, Najaf, Iraq; Karpagam Institute of Technology, Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering, Coimbatore, India; Dhanalakshmi Srinivasan College of Engineering and Technology, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Chennai, India; Dhanalakshmi Srinivasan College of Engineering, Coimbatore, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Coimbatore, India},
	abstract = {The rapid evolution of Industrial Internet of Things (IIoT) systems has introduced complex challenges related to data security, trust management, and reliable cloud integration. However, the existing Distributed Block Software Defined Cloud (DistB-SDCloud) with centralized architectures and static rule-based security models are inadequate for the dynamic, large-scale, and heterogeneous environments of Industry 4.0. To address these limitations, this paper proposes an Artificial Intelligence-Assisted Blockchain-SDCloud (AI-BSDCloud) Framework that employs SDN, Federated AI, and Blockchain technologies to provide a secure, scalable, and intelligent IIoT-cloud infrastructure. The proposed framework is a multi-layered framework where SDN is used for programmable flow control and isolation of devices. Next, a BlockChain is used to guarantee decentralization and maintain immutable transaction history, and AI assistive trust model to dynamically learn device behaviors via federated learning with anomaly detection. Additionally, smart contracts are used to direct access control and check logging capabilities. The AI-enabled trust model includes attack detection transforming the threat detection from static to dynamic. The attack detection engine is based on deep-learning techniques that applies to detect and mitigate attacks while the IIoT system is running. The framework is validated in the IIoT environment simulation with integration of OpenFlow, Ethereum Proof-of-Authority (PoA) blockchain, and cloud based RESTful APIs. Experimental results show that AI-BSDCloud provided the throughput (19.5 KB/s) based on number of nodes for securing industrial data exchange to improve operational resiliency. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
