	affiliations = {Chandigarh University, Department of CSE, Mohali, India},
	abstract = {The speed of healthcare digitalization requires a protected along with efficient framework to handle Electronic Health Records (EHRs). Traditional systems often struggle with disorganization, lack of clarity, and data breaches. This model solves primary healthcare data management problems by providing a dependable secure system for EHR management that protects user privacy during data exchange and management of Electronic Health Records ensuring regulatory compliances such as GDPR and HIPAA. This study develops a blockchain- operated conceptual model with Hyperledger Fabric to build a decentralized environment that secures healthcare information management. The enterprise-level features of Hyperledger Fabric combined with its permitted network architecture make it a secure solution for medical provider data exchange. The implementation process starts by installing core infrastructure through Docker and Docker Compose on cloud platforms, including AWS Azure or GCP. The system uses ECC and ZKP with MFA and an IAM framework to ensure strong security by enabling secure key creation, data protection, and enhanced user authorization. The React.js frontend engages in secure backend processes that handle data management operations alongside protected transaction functions that enable effective state control and secure storage of information. The implementation of IPFS off-chain storage solution improves system scalability alongside performance outcomes. Stealth Array ensures functional performance, data protection, and regulatory compliance such as GDPR and HIPAA. This model addresses healthcare data management difficulties to provide an effective approach for enhancing secure EHR management and security. Research should focus on deploying the model on real-world healthcare scenarios and optimize the model for scalability. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
