	affiliations = {Narasaraopeta Engineering College, Department of IT & CSE (AI), Narasaraopet, India; Aditya Institute of Technology and Management, Department of CSE, Tekkali, India},
	abstract = {In addition to providing helpful support in the form of data sharing, CC also provides funding. Information substance security also results from the transfer of the data to specific cloud workers. To improve access control over collective data and safeguard important and sensitive information, a number of procedures are employed. In this case, using ciphertext-policy attribute-based encryption (CP-ABE) approaches could be very advantageous and secure. While the traditional CP-ABE focuses solely on information privacy, clients’ personal security protection is currently a major concern. The CP-ABE by hidden access (HA) technique protects client privacy in addition to guaranteeing information privacy. However, the great majority of the existing plans are inefficient in terms of computation costs and overhead. Furthermore, the great majority of this system does not consider the issue of security spillover at the ability verification stage or ability authentication. This manuscript presents a security protected CP-ABE approach via proficient influence authentication to address the concerns mentioned above. Moreover, its privacy keys achieve uniform dimensions. The recommended plan addresses the decisional direct presumption and the specific safety in the interim. The numerical results validate the advantages of the proposed approach. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
