	abstract = {This research introduces the Comprehensive Data Access Protection Suite (CDAPS), an innovative approach to mitigating SQL injection (SQLi) attacks in web applications. CDAPS integrates three key components: honey tokens for early threat detection, dynamic privilege management for adaptive access control, and real-time monitoring for swift anomaly identification. By combining these elements, our system provides a multi-layered defense against evolving SQLi threats. Extensive testing across various attack scenarios demonstrates CDAPS's superior effectiveness in detecting and neutralizing SQLi at- tempts compared to traditional prevention methods. The system'sability to adapt to emerging threats and provide comprehensive logging for forensic analysis represents a significant advancement in database security. Our findings contribute to the field of web application security by offering a robust, integrated solution that not only enhances immediate threat response but also strengthenslong-term security posture. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
