	affiliations = {City University of Macau, Faculty of Data Science, Taipa, Macao; Fujian Normal University, College of Computer and Cyber Security, Fuzhou, China},
	abstract = {We propose a novel approach to utilize private set intersection (PSI) to achieve privacy-preserving authorization for IoT systems for the first time in this work. Our contribution includes an optimized PSI protocol that reduces communication costs and enhances privacy protection. The proposed protocol utilizes an aggregated algorithm to gain minimized communication overhead. Additionally, it achieves the size-hiding of the cloud platform's roles set with an optimized protocol. Specifically, we: (1) introduce a role-based access control framework that leverages PSI technology for IoT-focused system authorization; (2) optimize PSI communication complexity, resulting in ideal and constant costs regardless of the size of the role set of the two parties involved from the cloud platform to the IoT client, while maintaining linearity with the client's set size in the opposite direction, this significantly improves communication overhead for IoT systems; and (3) strengthen privacy protection concerning the cloud platform's set size. Overall, our proposed scheme enhances the practicality of IoT-focused system authorization while preserving privacy. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
