	affiliations = {Swami Rama Himalayan University, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Dehradun, India; University of Petroleum and Energy Studies, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Dehradun, India},
	abstract = {In this paper, we first explain the different cloud computing models and then elaborate on a detailed analysis of the problems associated with the cloud environment. However, due to the complexity of the cloud, it is difficult to achieve end-to-end security. This study also intends to investigate the cloud computing security concerns in public and private cloud-based environments and how they affect data security and may compromise data availability, confidentiality, and integrity. The article provides a thorough review of several cloud security concerns, such as data loss, insider threats, vendor lock-in, breaches of confidentiality, malicious assaults, and user ignorance. The security methods and solutions now in use to deal with these problems are also covered in the paper, including encryption, access control, monitoring, backup, and service level agreements (SLA). In this paper, the pros and cons of adopting a cloud are being evaluated based on the cost and security. The study examines the variables that institutions must take into account before deciding to use cloud computing from the perspective of cost and security. Most of the businesses are planning to shift to cloud computing but they are unable to even consider the possibility of having their confidential information off-site. The study does not claim that cloud computing is the best option for all situations, but whether or not to use it should be determined by a thorough investigation. Finally, in order to guarantee the security and privacy of data stored on the cloud, the study concludes by highlighting the significance of user and cloud service provider cooperation. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
