	year = {2024},
	pages = {},
	doi = {10.1109/NMITCON62075.2024.10699273},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85207405146&doi=10.1109%2FNMITCON62075.2024.10699273&partnerID=40&md5=24ff86f5aa85bbfe2b318f6a482a859d},
	affiliations = {E.G.S Pillay Engineering College, Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering, Nagapattinam, India; Nitte Meenakshi Institute of Technology, Department of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Bengaluru, India; M.Kumarasamy College of Engineering, Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering, Karur, India},
	abstract = {In a distributed system environment, cloud computing describes a new technology that lets customers pay for the services they utilize as needed. Cloud service companies that prioritize maximum security supply a plethora of resources, including Infrastructure, Software, Platform, and Database. The literature has a wealth of security measures, such as Service Level Agreements (SLAs), access control rules, and cryptographic methods. This work implements a novel compound data encryption technique called Data Security in Cloud Computing using Maritime Search and Rescue Algorithm (DSCC-MSRA). It integrates the advantages of an enhanced cypher block chaining algorithm having logical substitution with an optimization algorithm called MSRA for key generation. This encryption method uses a different algorithm for generating keys. This method is optimized to a reasonable degree by running it through a variety of security as well as statistical analyses. This ground-breaking method is compared to currently used, widely used algorithms in the industry. This technique aims to enhance the encryption procedure and complicate the cryptanalysis procedure. The proposed system provided a better result in accuracy, efficiency, and encryption when compared with existing methods like CNN, C-DSS. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
