	affiliations = {St.Joseph's Institute of Technology, Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering, Chennai, India},
	abstract = {In recent healthcare research, there has been a significant focus on integrating emerging technologies such as Blockchain, IoT, and cloud computing. This paper introduces BCGeo, a novel architecture for decentralized geospatial services specifically tailored for smart healthcare systems. Addressing the limitations of traditional healthcare systems, BCGeo presents an online geospatial healthcare service designed for international residents of Bhubaneswar, India. The framework systematically tackles crucial technological issues, including data gathering, processing, access control, and privacy protection. BCGeo enhances healthcare service delivery through features like scalability, geospatial mapping, immutability, and patient prioritization. An analytical queueing system ensures efficient resource utilization, prioritizing urgent patient treatment. Decentralized privacy protection policies, enabled by Blockchain consensus, validate and anonymize data. Performance analysis, supported by detailed graphs and experimental data, verifies the efficiency of the proposed design. BCGeo marks a significant advancement in healthcare system design, offering an intelligent, accessible, and secure solution to contemporary healthcare challenges. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
