	year = {2024},
	pages = {},
	doi = {10.1109/ICICET59348.2024.10616375},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85201198670&doi=10.1109%2FICICET59348.2024.10616375&partnerID=40&md5=a8269475b3336ffdf488365f49c7225f},
	affiliations = {G.H. Raisoni College of Engineering, Nagpur, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Nagpur, India; G.H. Raisoni College of Engineering, Nagpur, Department of Dic, Nagpur, India},
	abstract = {The Data Defender's Shield is a powerful protector that uses a variety of techniques to protect data, including advanced encryption and access control. This state-of-the-art solution is intended to strengthen cloud-based platform integrity, guaranteeing that private data is protected from unauthorised access. Modern encryption algorithms are fundamentally used by the Data Defender's Shield to build an impregnable fortress around the digital assets it protects. This mastery of cryptography guarantees that, even in the case of a breach, the compromised data cannot be decoded, hence reducing possible dangers and safeguarding the privacy of vital data. The shield also uses dynamic access management protocols, which give organisations fine-grained control over who may access particular data sets and when. Moreover, the Data Defender's Shield offers a seamless user experience without sacrificing security by integrating with cloud-based apps. Because of its adaptability, businesses can keep up with changing cyberthreats by continuously improving and modifying their defences against new attacks. By means of the well-balanced combination of sophisticated encryption and access control, this technical marvel acts as a formidable guardian, enabling businesses to take use of the cloud's boundless potential while safeguarding their most precious resource. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
