	affiliations = {Tagore Engineering College, Department of Artificial Intelligence and Data Science, Chennai, India; RMK College of Engineering and Technology, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Thiruvallur, India; S.A. Engineering College, Chennai, India; Saveetha School of Engineering, Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering, Chennai, India; Chennai Institute of Technology, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Chennai, India; SRM Institute of Science and Technology, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Kattankulathur, India},
	abstract = {In this study, an efficient system to improve the oxygen supply in hospitals and other healthcare institutions is proposed. It uses Internet of things (IoT) devices and cloud based data transmission and processing system. The controller unit collects the oxygen sensor data for the analysis and uses HTTP protocols to send and receive data with cloud computing in HTTP website server. The cloud is data storage, processes and real-time monitoring, analysis and control system. It has a user interface with viewed administrators and medical professionals. The interface provides real-time data regarding oxygen supply, consumption patterns, and possible concerns. Authorized workers can access and manage the system via the display, allowing for timely adjustments to oxygen supply settings, optimizations to refill schedules, and responses to emergency circumstances. It's adaptable, flexible, and resilient, which are benefits. There will be less need to worry about oxygen shortages and interruptions, and healthcare institutions of all sizes can benefit from this. The cloud's remote access and control capabilities provide continuous functioning and rapid reaction times. It's an effective solution for hospitals and other healthcare facilities that need to control their oxygen supplies. With its cloud-based design, the solution increases productivity, improves patient safety, and simplifies oxygen management. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
