	affiliations = {Putian University, Putian, China; Ltd., Fuzhou, China; Minnan Normal University, School of Computer Science, Zhangzhou, China},
	abstract = {Cloud storage service enables users not only to save their local data storage costs but also to access their outsourced data at any time and anywhere. Traditionally, a data owner outsources the encrypted data to the cloud server and then checks its integrity with the help of cloud auditing strategies. Obviously, in such a manner, only confidentiality and integrity are considered following the above two independent steps. Furthermore, it becomes an issue that the data owner may want to share their outsourced data with some authorized data receivers and convince them that the data are from and the same as the data owner's. To solve this issue, absorbing the advantage of the certificateless cryptosystem, we propose an efficient certificateless proxy re-signcryption (CLPRSC) for data access control in cloud computing. Moreover, the CLPRSC possesses ciphertext verifiable, convertible, and designated re-signcryptable properties with the highest efficiency among the achievable signcryption with proxy re-encryption schemes, which may be of independent interest. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
