	abstract = {This research examines the influence of the use of cloud computing on data management, with a specific emphasis on its ability to provide scalable solutions for storage and processing. The methodological approach involves doing a thorough assessment of existing literature and analyzing secondary data sources in order to provide a full overview of the topic matter. A systematic literature review was used to collect pertinent research results and data pertaining to the impact of cloud computing on data management. This approach facilitates the amalgamation of preexisting information and perspectives from many sources. The observations indicate that cloud computing has revolutionized data management by providing scalable and adaptable choices for both storage and processing. It has empowered enterprises to effectively manage substantial amounts of data and use computational resources as needed. Nevertheless, the ease and accessibility of cloud computing can give rise to difficulties in the confidentiality and protection of data. To address these difficulties, it is essential to implement encryption, and access control, and comply with data protection rules. The research concludes that cloud computing has fundamentally transformed data management, providing firms with robust tools to efficiently handle data. Nevertheless, it entails the need to employ resilient data privacy and security safeguards. Organizations should give priority to implementing measures such as encryption and access control in order to safeguard sensitive data. Adhering to legislation such as GDPR is crucial for maintaining trust and complying with legal obligations. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
