	abstract = {The Internet of Things (IoT) is swiftly infiltrating essential sectors, facilitating widespread interconnection and utilization of a wide range of devices while simultaneously processing massive amounts of data. In face of this rapid change, data security has brought critical challenges in the design and implementation of IoT applications. However, resource limitations and the diverse nature of IoT devices often make traditional encryption methods ineffective or impractical for ensuring secure data transmission. As a result, there is an urgent need to create and implement lightweight, secure, and scalable solutions for data communication that can effectively address these challenges. In this paper, through simulation experiments and comparative analysis with related security schemes, the authors demonstrate the effectiveness and efficiency of Lightweight Secure Data Transmission. The comparison results reveal that the proposed scheme outperforms other related schemes in terms of communication and computing costs, making it a highly suitable and efficient option for IoT applications. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
