	abstract = {The Wide spread use of cloud storage services and their demonstrated power provide the foundational underpinning for the cloud computing industry rapid development. Nevertheless, a lot of security incidents still occur at the cloud storage layer due to deliberate attacks and management negligence, resulting in significant leaks of critical data. To address the issue, we inculate AES and Cryptographic Pseudo Random Number Generator Algorithms. The proposed standard illustrates the process of dividing the data into segments which is encrypted with aes individually to ensure the strong security for data. By distributing the scattered data segments among several cloud sites, security is improved and the possibility of a single point of failure is decreased. Securing access control mechanisms makes it easy for authorized individuals to access and decode data. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
