	affiliations = {Ramaiah Institute of Technology, Department of Information Science and Engineering, Bengaluru, India; Hindusthan Institute of Technology, Coimbatore, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Coimbatore, India; Presidency University Bangalore, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Bengaluru, India},
	abstract = {Many institutions now do not have a platform where students can view all of the offers from various firms, and they must fill out the form with their information again for each company that visits. To minimize future problems, the college placement department must check each student's information. Companies rely on the Placement department to obtain information about selected applicants for additional procedures. To solve this problem, a platform for students to register and submit their updated profiles was required. Companies can see the applications received for a specific job vacancy, admin can approve or reject the student's registration based on the database present with him, and students can see various job openings from companies at a specific time. The current system is not a proper and appropriate method of implementing Training and Placement management because it becomes difficult for the placement department to manage all of the databases, send emails regarding offers to every student, and keep track of every student, whether they received an offer or not. As a result, this study created a platform for students to register and submit their updated profiles, reducing administrative effort. Companies get immediate access to the applications submitted for a specific employment opportunity. Features are supplied to immediately generate information from existing data. This study recommended segmenting the web app into three components for design: admin, company, and student. React JS is utilized as a frontend framework for development, Node JS as a server-side script for integration and REST operations, MongoDB and Mongoose for databases and connections, Redux for state management, and Axios for requests and answers. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
