	abstract = {In this current digital world, the term 'Cloud' represents limitless possibilities. It refers to a large network of computers that use the Internet to store, process, and manage data and services. This provides unmatched scalability and accessibility, and it is cost-efficient. Most simply, it is the delivery of on-demand IT Resources like storage, network, and databases of our choice over the internet. However, the adaptation of cloud resources has raised problems like data security, compliance, data privacy, downtime, and availability of the cloud. This article mainly focuses on the challenges in cloud security and presents some of its probable solutions to reduce the risks caused by cloud security issues. The research study starts out by outlining cloud security and going over the various cloud security concerns. The best behaviors for protecting cloud data are further explained, including using strong passwords and multi-factor authentication, encrypting data while it's in transit and at rest, as well as putting access control policies. By recognizing these problems, and by applying the most effective security measures, organizations/businesses can safely take advantage of cloud computing. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
