	affiliations = {Sri Ramakrishna Engineering College, Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering, Coimbatore, India},
	abstract = {This paper presents a research project focusing on enhancing security features in cloud access through the utilization of AES (Advanced Encryption Standard) algorithms. The primary objective of this project is to ensure the easy accessibility of data and applications exclusively for authorized users. To address the prevalent privacy concerns in cloud access systems, we propose a novel distributed data access control mechanism that aims to safeguard user privacy. The first component of our approach introduces a groundbreaking method for achieving user anonymity, specifically targeting collusion scenarios involving untrustworthy authorities. The second component features a state-of-the-art policy obfuscation mechanism that effectively protects the confidentiality of decision attributes (metadata) from conspiring parties. Furthermore, we introduce a third-party authority system as the third component of our privacy enhancements, allowing authorities to log in and out of the system without overriding each other's permissions. Additionally, we propose a new activation feature and conduct a comparative analysis against popular activation features such as VM Orchestrator, VMware Sphere, and Ovirt, with the objective of enhancing system performance and security. Through this project, we aim to contribute to the ongoing efforts in strengthening the security framework of cloud access systems while ensuring user privacy. © 2023 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
