	affiliations = {COMSATS University Islamabad, Department of Computer Science, Islamabad, Pakistan},
	abstract = {Data storage is transitioning from physical servers to 'cloud' storage because cloud service providers deliver the resources through the Internet when required. Cloud computing is a successful and rapidly evolving technology. With new features and capabilities released regularly, companies can move to the cloud on a 'pay as you go' model. The most prominent feature of pay as you go model on the cloud is that it is cost-effective, however, this makes the cloud platform vulnerable to cyber attacks. This is the reason, the safety of such information has become a concern. This paper provides a security framework that secures cloud storage from unauthorized individuals by using user identification and authorization. We have used dual encryption by using Advance encryption standard (AES) & Ecliptic Curve Cryptography (ECC). The double encryption makes the cloud environment resilient against different security attacks. The experimental results show that the proposed model has low computing costs. © 2023 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
