	affiliations = {Institut Penyelidikan dan Kemajuan Pertanian Malaysia, Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia},
	abstract = {This paper describes the development of a portable biosensor platform equipped with an electrochemical interface and an IoT cloud system. An Android-based portable device was installed with a developed electrochemical software where it served as an electrochemical reader and also able to display results on the same screen. A GPS tracking was included in the device to pinpoint the location of the analysis performed, especially during field testing. The device was also linked with cloud system which can be accessed through a dedicated website. The website served as platform for electrochemical and authorisation settings, as well as data storage. Data and information breach can be minimized as it only permitted authorised and registered personnel to access this cloud system. The developed portable electrochemical reader then was applied for in-situ detection of multi-mycotoxins using a functionalized three-electrode-system screen-printed carbon electrode (SPCE) as the sensing medium; was attached to the reader. Standard curves for aflatoxin B1, ochratoxin A and fumonisin B1 in grain corn matrix were successfully developed using the SPCEs and developed prototype. The application of the portable reader was eventually tested on grain corn field in Chuping, Perlis for aflatoxin B1 detection. © 2022 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
