	affiliations = {Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar Marathwada University, Department of Computer Science and IT, Aurangabad, India},
	abstract = {Users lose responsibility for personal information whenever they upload their data to the Cloud. The growth of cloud computing would be hampered if indeed the cloud environment fails to produce an appropriate security mechanism to ensure data security. Throughout the intervening decades, access control and encryption methods were unable to properly restrict the spread of private tenant data within the platform. The intricacy of the cloud infrastructure limits the necessary information flow control paradigm, and protecting private data stored in the Cloud becomes challenging. A literature study is conducted in this research program as a first step toward constructing an innovative and secured information flow control in a cloud environment. In this research paper, the most exciting researchers on Cloud information flow control framed by various researchers worldwide are gathered and assessed. The articles are examined regarding security techniques and their benefits and cons. In addition, the service type, information flow direction, and performance recorded by each of the works are discussed. Furthermore, existing models’ research gaps and problems are highlighted to inspire future Cloud-based information flow control researchers. © 2022 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
