	title = {SECURE WEB ACCESSIBILITY PROTOCOL FOR CHALLENGED USERS},
	year = {2021},
	pages = {},
	doi = {10.1109/ICCCNT51525.2021.9579875},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85126266148&doi=10.1109%2FICCCNT51525.2021.9579875&partnerID=40&md5=65f3dde2530fb30bbcd54df6a51706ce},
	affiliations = {COEP Technological University, Pune, Department of Computer Engineering and IT, Pune, India},
	abstract = {An unsolved problem in the domain of Internet Accessibility, which is a stream in Human Computer Interface (HCI), is how cognitively challenged or visually impaired users access a service. This paper proposes an assistive technology for disabled users in the form of a Randomized Authentication Gateway (RAG) mechanism corresponding to a challenge-pool. The challenge-pool contains different stand-alone Accessibility Protocols that are suitable for different situations. Holistically, we believe that the system works the finest when it is used as a single federated interface. The RAG manager picks up random challenges from the challenge-pool and the client, who is looking to access a particular service, is subjected to these challenges. If the client successfully completes them, he is authenticated as a valid user of the intended service. This paper discusses the audio-based, pressure-based and gesture-based mechanisms for seamless authentication of challenged users. We have defined this problem in terms of Accessibility Deficiency and Bot Indicator. The proposed system is only 23% accessibility deficient and covers the use cases of partially blind, completely blind, color blind and users suffering from diseases that affects their comprehension skills, like dyslexia. The research focuses on a keyboard-friendly environment where the fit or challenged users will have complete control over the interface using the one-click functionality. This work is our way to ensure that no restriction is imposed on any user while surfing through the internet. © 2022 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
	author_keywords = {Assistive Technology; Authentication; Authorization; Random Media; Security Protocol; Web Service},
