	affiliations = {Sirindhorn International Institute of Technology Thammasat University, Computer, Khlong Luang, Thailand},
	abstract = {Owing to the cryptographic-based access control property, ciphertext policy attribute-based encryption (CP-ABE) has been widely adopted as an effective solution for data access control in cloud computing. Nevertheless, CP-ABE cryptographic construct is based on bilinear paring rendering high computation cost. Therefore, using CP-ABE in MCC environment is non-trivial because mobile devices are resource-constraint (such as limited battery, limited computing power) and they are not suitable to run such high complexity of crypto operation. This research issue is unmatured and requires in-depth investigation. In this paper, we investigate the research problems and challenges of data access control in mobile cloud computing (MCC). Specifically, we conduct the comprehensive review of existing solutions based on CP-ABE. The review is done through the analysis and discussion of recent solutions. We also provide the comparative analysis of the selected works. Finally, we point out possible research issues and challenges. © 2021 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
